2026-11-04T20:13:06.969056372Z WARNING: POSTGRES_HOST_AUTH_METHOD has been set to "trust". This will allow
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969063083Z          anyone with access to the Postgres port to access your database without
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969067192Z          a password, even if POSTGRES_PASSWORD is set. See PostgreSQL
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969071108Z          documentation about "trust":
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969075198Z          https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/auth-trust.html
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969079085Z          In Docker's default configuration, this is effectively any other
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969083436Z          container on the same system.
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969087294Z 
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969090865Z          It is not recommended to use POSTGRES_HOST_AUTH_METHOD=trust. Replace
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969094814Z          it with "-e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=password" instead to set a password in
2026-11-04T20:13:06.969098964Z          "docker run".
